BalanceNG 3.168 is now available at http://www.BalanceNG.net
Release-Date: September 22, 2010

----

Changes:

* The IPv6 mask6 directive is no longer restricted to be on byte boundary.

* The link detection mechanisms for Solaris on SPARC have been improved for e1000g and nxge interfaces.

* The manual has been updated accordingly:
  http://www.inlab.de/balanceng/BalanceNG-V3-Manual.pdf

----

BalanceNG V3 Examples

* SIP/UDP load-balancing with Call-ID session management
  http://www.inlab.de/balanceng/example10.html

* IPv6 SLB (Server Load-Balancing) in DSR mode
  http://www.inlab.de/balanceng/example11.html

* IPv6 SLB (Server Load-Balancing) in DSR mode with agent feedback 
  http://www.inlab.de/balanceng/example12.html

* IPv6 SLB (Server Load-Balancing) multiple legged with VRRP tracking
  http://www.inlab.de/balanceng/example13.html

* IPv6 SLB (Server Load-Balancing) with dual stack NAT 
  http://www.inlab.de/balanceng/example14.html

* IPv4 LLB (Link Load-Balancing)
  http://www.inlab.de/balanceng/example15.html

----

About BalanceNG:

BalanceNG is an IPv6 capable software load-balancer and runs on Linux and Solaris operating systems. BalanceNG is the core load-balancing engine of the SECUDOS and Thomas-Krenn load-balancer appliances.

About Inlab Software GmbH:

Inlab Software GmbH, founded in 1991 is an ISV (Independent Software Vendor) located in Gruenwald near Munich, Germany. Inlab focuses on networking system software, load-balancing software, programming languages and security software. Inlab develops software for Linux and Solaris operating systems and develops both commercial products and Open-Source software.

----

OEM-Partner BalanceNG certified systems:

* Available Worldwide:
  The SECUDOS Load-Balancer (SLB) Product Family
  http://www.secudos.com/metadot/index.pl?id=4703;isa=Category;op=show

* Available in Europe:
  Thomas-Krenn LoadBalancer (TKLB)
  http://www.thomas-krenn.com/en/further-areas/load-balancer.html

