BalanceNG 3.172 is now available at http://www.BalanceNG.net
Release-Date: August 24, 2010

----

Changes:

* IPv6 location support has been implemented.

* A recent version of the IPv6 range .csv file (IpToCounty.6R.csv) is now part of the BalanceNG V3 distribution.

* The command ipdb6 has been implemented to load the IPv6 in memory location database from a 5-column .csv file (as in IpToCounty.6R.csv).

* The "locate" command has been extended to accept IPv6 addresses.

* The location group mechanisms have been extended to support IPv6 load balancing decisions based on the location of the IPv6 client IP address.

* The manual has been updated accordingly.

----

Here's the newest online example explaining IPv6 SLB (Server Load-
Balancing) in DSR mode with BalanceNG V3: http://www.inlab.de/balanceng/example11.html

----

About BalanceNG:

BalanceNG is an IPv6 capable software load-balancer and runs on Linux and Solaris operating systems. BalanceNG is the core load-balancing engine of the SECUDOS and Thomas-Krenn load-balancer appliances.

About Inlab Software GmbH:

Inlab Software GmbH, founded in 1991 is an ISV (Independent Software Vendor) located in Gruenwald near Munich, Germany. Inlab focuses on networking system software, load-balancing software, programming languages and security software. Inlab develops software for Linux and Solaris operating systems and develops both commercial products and Open-Source software.

----

Best Regards,
Thomas Obermair
Inlab Software GmbH

----

